Hecks.hecksagon "Pizzas" do
  capabilities :crud

  # ============================================================
  # The async boundary — declared here, never in the domain.
  # ============================================================
  #
  # The Order aggregate's domain logic (pizzas.bluebook) is purely
  # synchronous : PlaceOrder validates and emits OrderPlaced, full
  # stop. The CHARGE — a remote call with latency, timeouts, retries,
  # a flaky gateway — lives entirely in this one adapter. The verdict
  # re-enters the domain as a plain Order.Authorize / Order.Decline
  # command (the result_into shape). No tokio, no Mutex, no channel
  # ever reaches aggregate code ; the adapter owns all of it.
  #
  # WHERE the gateway lives (endpoint, timeout, retry budget) is
  # per-deployment config — it lives in pizzas.world, not here. This
  # hecksagon declares the WIRING shape ; the world supplies the
  # location. Same split as :heki (adapter here, dir in .world).
  #
  # The handwritten Rust projection of this boundary — the sync port /
  # async worker / re-entry bridge the code generator should emit —
  # lives beside this file under adapters/.
  adapter :shell, name: :payment_gateway,
          trigger_on: "OrderPlaced",
          result_into: "Order.Authorize | Order.Decline",
          command: "bin/charge-gateway",
          args: ["{{ref}}", "{{quantity}}"]

  # ============================================================
  # Persistence — the ADAPTER specifies the port ; the world configures it.
  # ============================================================
  #
  # The Order / Pizza aggregates (pizzas.bluebook) talk to the persistence
  # PORT (back_aggregate_storage) ; the BLUEBOOK never names a store. THIS
  # hecksagon — the wiring, not the domain — binds the port to :heki. WHICH
  # store is the adapter's job ; the per-deployment VALUE (the .heki dir) is
  # CONFIG in pizzas.world (heki do dir "pizzas/.heki" end). Same split as
  # the payment adapter : adapter here, endpoint/timeout in the world.
  # Default (no persistence adapter) is memory + sync ; :heki / :sqlite are
  # the overrides. Swap stores by changing this one line.
  adapter :heki

  # ============================================================
  # Reporting — a distinct adapter off the render_report port.
  # ============================================================
  #
  # The domain declares the QUERY (Order.Pending) ; it is format-blind. The
  # ADAPTER is the format : :html serves the pending-orders report at /orders,
  # its sibling :markdown would render the SAME query as markdown (a chained
  # report). Presentation is not domain — the bluebook never knows about HTML.
  adapter :html, query: "Pizzas::Order.pending", get: "/orders"
end
